{%- from "partials/icons.njk" import arrow -%}

<section class="sec">
  <div class="wrap">
    <div class="svc-layout">
      <div class="svc-body prose rv">

        <h2 id="enquiry">The enquiry form</h2>
        <p>If you submit the form on the <a href="{{ '/contact/' | url }}">contact page</a>, the details you
          enter — your name, organisation, email address, phone number, the sector and service you selected,
          the site location and your message — are sent to us by email so that we can reply to you.</p>
        <p>We use those details only to respond to your enquiry and to carry out any work that follows from it.
          We do not sell them, and we do not add you to a mailing list.</p>
        {%- if enquiry.active %}
        <p>The message is delivered by
          {%- if enquiry.provider == "web3forms" %} Web3Forms
          {%- elif enquiry.provider == "formspree" %} Formspree
          {%- elif enquiry.provider == "formsubmit" %} FormSubmit
          {%- else %} a third-party form-delivery service
          {%- endif %}, which passes it on to our inbox. It travels over an encrypted
          connection and is not used for any other purpose.</p>
        {%- else %}
        <p>The form is not yet connected to a delivery service. Until it is, submitting it opens your own
          email application with the details filled in, so nothing is sent anywhere until you send it
          yourself.</p>
        {%- endif %}
        <p>Enquiries that lead to no engagement are kept only as long as they are useful for following up,
          and deleted after that. If you would rather not use the form at all, call
          {%- for p in site.contact.phones %}
          <a href="tel:{{ p.e164 }}">{{ p.display }}</a>{% if not loop.last %} or{% endif %}
          {%- endfor %} or email
          <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact.email }}">{{ site.contact.email }}</a>.</p>

        <h2 id="third">Third parties this site loads</h2>
        <p>Three things on this site are served by other companies. Each of them can see your IP address and
          your browser's user-agent string, as any web server can, because that is how a request reaches them.</p>
        <ul>
          <li><strong>Google Fonts</strong> — the typefaces used across the site are requested from
            <code>fonts.googleapis.com</code> and <code>fonts.gstatic.com</code> on every page.</li>
          <li><strong>Esri</strong> — the map on the contact page loads its tiles from Esri's ArcGIS
            Online service, built from OpenStreetMap, HERE and Garmin data. It is loaded only when you
            scroll near it, and only on that page. If you follow the "open in Google Maps" link, that is
            a visit to Google like any other.</li>
          <li><strong>Our hosting provider</strong> — like any web host, it keeps short-lived server logs of
            requests, which include IP addresses.</li>
        </ul>
        <p>None of these are used by us for analytics or profiling. We do not run Google Analytics, any
          advertising pixel, or any other tracker on this site.</p>

        <h2 id="cookies">Cookies and tracking</h2>
        <p>This site sets no cookies of its own, stores nothing in your browser, and shows no consent banner
          because there is nothing to consent to. There is no session, no login and no account.</p>

        <h2 id="rights">Your information</h2>
        <p>If you have sent us an enquiry and want to know what we hold, want it corrected, or want it
          deleted, write to <a href="mailto:{{ site.contact.email }}">{{ site.contact.email }}</a> from the
          address you used, or call us. We will act on it.</p>
        <p>{{ site.name }}, {{ site.contact.addressFull }}.</p>

        <p style="margin-top:34px;color:var(--muted-2);font-size:13.5px">This page describes the website. It
          is not a contract, and it does not cover information you give us directly by phone, email or during
          an engagement — that is governed by the terms of the engagement itself.</p>
      </div>

